{"museum":"Q7370843","name":"Rough Point","checked":"2026-11-05","source":"Newport Restoration Foundation website; OpenStreetMap","onViewKnown":false,"note":"Rough Point was Doris Duke’s Newport home, left as she lived in it: Old Master paintings, tapestries and French furniture beside 1980s phones and appliances. This guide lists the rooms, every highlight the Newport Restoration Foundation publishes from the collection (placed in a room only when NRF names it) and the 2026 exhibitions. The house is open through November 8, then for “A Rough Point Holiday” on weekends from November 27 to December 27.","works":[{"id":"rp-rough-point-from-the-drive","title":"Rough Point from the drive","artist":"Rough Point","medium":"Historic place","url":"https://www.newportrestoration.org/programs-initiatives/telling-stories-dispersed-monument/rough-point/","imageUrl":"data/roughpoint/images/rp-rough-point-from-the-drive.jpg","onView":true,"gallery":"House","floor":"G"},{"id":"rp-the-ocean-front-of-rough-point","title":"The ocean front of Rough Point","artist":"Rough Point","medium":"Historic place","url":"https://www.newportrestoration.org/programs-initiatives/telling-stories-dispersed-monument/rough-point/","imageUrl":"data/roughpoint/images/rp-the-ocean-front-of-rough-point.jpg","onView":true,"gallery":"House","floor":"G"},{"id":"rp-the-lions-terrace","title":"The lions terrace","artist":"Rough Point","medium":"Historic place","url":"https://www.newportrestoration.org/programs-initiatives/telling-stories-dispersed-monument/rough-point/","imageUrl":"data/roughpoint/images/rp-the-lions-terrace.jpg","onView":true,"gallery":"Ocean Terrace","floor":"G"},{"id":"rp-the-olmsted-landscape-and-arboretum","title":"The Olmsted landscape and arboretum","artist":"Rough Point","medium":"Garden","url":"https://www.newportrestoration.org/programs-initiatives/telling-stories-dispersed-monument/rough-point/","imageUrl":"data/roughpoint/images/rp-the-olmsted-landscape-and-arboretum.jpg","onView":t